# World-class dashboard UI implementation pass

This pass turns the dashboard into a more premium, product-grade analytics experience while preserving the existing FastAPI + vanilla JavaScript architecture and the Domo-first CSAT source model.

## What changed

### Shared UX system

The repeated UI logic is now centralized in shared assets instead of being copied into every page:

- `assets/dashboard_ux.css`
- `assets/dashboard_ux.js`
- `GET /assets/dashboard_ux.css`
- `GET /assets/dashboard_ux.js`

This makes the UI layer easier to upgrade without editing `index.html`, `csat.html`, and `starter_guides.html` separately.

### Premium visual redesign

The shared CSS adds a more polished dashboard shell:

- executive-grade hero area on every page
- glass/sticky header treatment
- redesigned card, KPI, table, and chart surfaces
- better spacing, hover states, focus states, radius, and shadow hierarchy
- dark mode
- compact analyst density mode
- presentation mode
- responsive mobile/tablet behavior
- reduced-motion support
- improved keyboard focus styling
- skip-to-dashboard accessibility link

### Universal chart experience

Every detected Chart.js canvas now gets the same chart actions automatically:

- `Insight` local analyst readout
- `Data` table view
- `CSV` export
- `PNG` export
- `Focus` mode
- click-to-inspect point popover
- keyboard Enter/Space opens focus mode
- shared chart focus studio
- combined export for all loaded chart data

The UX engine detects charts dynamically with a `MutationObserver`, so charts that render later after API calls still get upgraded.

### Command center and navigation

Every page now has:

- command palette opened with Cmd/Ctrl+K
- quick navigation to Portal, CSAT, and Starter Guides
- theme, density, presentation, and export actions
- generated on-page section map
- chart count/status tiles
- page-specific source and quality copy

### CSAT source model preserved

The CSAT UI remains Domo-first:

- no visible Excel upload workflow
- no `/upload/csat` usage in `csat.html`
- Domo refresh remains the intended operational path
- raw call details remain protected
- public CSAT aggregate view remains sanitized

### Testability improvements

Added `test_ui_experience.py` to protect the new UI contract:

- shared UX assets are linked on every dashboard page
- universal chart actions exist
- chart canvases exist for all dashboard surfaces
- CSAT remains Domo-first rather than upload-first
- accessibility/power-user controls are present
- shared assets are served by the backend with expected content types

Also hardened refresh/cache endpoints for automated tests so they do not spawn long-running network refresh tasks under test mode.

## Chart coverage

Static dashboard canvases currently covered by the shared chart UX engine:

| Page | Chart canvases covered |
|---|---:|
| Portal Activity | 9 |
| Call Quality / CSAT | 9 |
| Starter Guides | 6 |
| **Total** | **24** |

The engine is dynamic, so future Chart.js canvases added to these pages will automatically receive the same toolbar and focus behavior as long as they have an `id`.

