python3 -m py_compile main.py
node --check assets/dashboard_ux.js
python3 /tmp/check_html_scripts.py
pytest -q
```

Result:

```text
73 passed
```

## Remaining next-level investments

This pass is a major UI/product upgrade while staying inside the current stack. The next major leap would be:

1. Move frontend pages into a component system or module-based build pipeline.
2. Add Playwright browser tests with screenshots for desktop/tablet/mobile states.
3. Add true chart brushing/zooming with a Chart.js zoom plugin or custom range selector.
4. Add saved dashboard views and shareable URL filter state.
5. Add role-based permissions instead of a single admin token.
6. Move metric definitions into a backend semantic layer with typed Pydantic response models.
